  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Naresh Pandurang Mhatre vs State Of Maharashtra on 13 July, 2022 Author: N. J. Jamadar Bench: N. J. Jamadar 906-Aba-1891-22.Doc Sayali Upasani In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Criminal Appellate Jurisdiction Santosh Anticipatory Bail Application No. 1891 Of 2022 Subhash Kulkarni Digitally signed by Naresh Pandurang Mhatre ...Applicant Santosh Subhash Kulkarni Date: 2022.07.15 Versus 11:48:29 +0530 State of Maharashtra ... Respondent Mr. Vishal Kolekar i/b Kishan Chaudhari, for the Applicant. Smt. M.R. Tidke, App for the State/Respondent. Coram: N. J. Jamadar, J. Dated: 13th July, 2022 Order:",
    "facts": "By this application, the applicant is seeking the relief of pre- arrest bail under Section 438 of the Code of Criminal Procedure, 1973 (for short \"Cr.P.C.\"), as he apprehends arrest in connection with Crime Register No.129 of 2022 registered with Alibaug Police Station, Raigad. The offences alleged against him are punishable under Sections 328, 272, 273, 188 read with Section 34 of the Indian Penal Code, 1860 (for short \"IPC\"), and also under Sections 26(1), 26(2)(ii), 26(2)(iv), 26(3), 30(2)(a), and 59 of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006. As per the prosecution, the informant, one Vishwajit Vithhal Shinde, who is a Food Inspector, conducted a series of raids on 31 May 2022 along with his team and a panch witness. The first raid was carried out at around 4:30 p.m. at M/s Ashoka Pan Stall, 903-aba-1891-2022.doc Alibaug. The second raid followed at about 5:20 p.m. at M/s Rupa Pan Shop, Alibaug. The third raid was conducted at about 6:10 p.m. at M/s I Love Alibaug Pan Shop, Alibaug. During these raids, the team seized prohibited and banned substances such as Vimal Pan Masala, scented tobacco, Manikchand Gutkha, and Kesaryukt Goa. Based on these seizures, an FIR was lodged against the present applicant, alleging his involvement in the storage and sale of such contraband. 3. The learned Advocate appearing for the applicant submitted that the applicant has extended full co-operation during the course of investigation. It is pointed out that the charge-sheet has already been filed, which shows that the investigation is complete. It is further submitted that this Court had granted interim protection by its order dated 13 July 2022.",
    "arguments": "The said protection has been continued from time to time and is still operative. The applicant has scrupulously abided by the conditions imposed by this Court while granting ad-interim protection and has not misused the [LEAKAGE_MASK]. On these grounds, it is prayed that the interim relief granted earlier be confirmed and continued. 4. On the other hand, the learned APP opposed the application. It is argued that the material collected during investigation prima facie indicates the applicant's involvement in the alleged offences. It is therefore submitted that this is not a fit case to grant anticipatory bail and the application deserves rejection. 903-aba-1891-2022.doc c) The applicant shall not directly or indirectly make any inducement, threat or promise to any witness acquainted with the facts of the case so as to dissuade him from disclosing such facts to the court or to any police officer.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "The said protection has been continued from time to time and is still operative. The applicant has scrupulously abided by the conditions imposed by this Court while granting ad-interim protection and has not misused the [LEAKAGE_MASK]. On these grounds, it is prayed that the interim relief granted earlier be confirmed and continued. 4. On the other hand, the learned APP opposed the application. It is argued that the material collected during investigation prima facie indicates the applicant's involvement in the alleged offences. It is therefore submitted that this is not a fit case to grant anticipatory bail and the application deserves rejection.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": "903-aba-1891-2022.doc c) The applicant shall not directly or indirectly make any inducement, threat or promise to any witness acquainted with the facts of the case so as to dissuade him from disclosing such facts to the court or to any police officer."
  },
